# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values below.
# Only DASHBOARD_PASSWORD and GITHUB_TOKEN are required to run on your Mac.
#
# When the dashboard runs on AWS (ECS), none of these live in a file — they
# come from SSM Parameter Store SecureStrings under /loop-dashboard/, injected
# by the task definition's "secrets" block (infra/task-definition.json). Never
# put a secret in the task definition's "environment" block: that value is
# readable by anyone who can call ecs:DescribeTaskDefinition.
#
# Deployed right now: DASHBOARD_PASSWORD and SESSION_SECRET. GITHUB_TOKEN is
# deliberately NOT deployed — see infra/deploy.sh.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required --

# The single password you type on the /login screen. Pick something long and
# random. (It used to double as the cookie-signing key; SESSION_SECRET below
# now does that job, so changing your password no longer logs everyone out.)
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-long-random-password

# A GitHub fine-grained Personal Access Token (PAT) with READ + WRITE access
# to the ApagPlayz/content-generation-platform repository.
#
# Repository permissions it needs:
#   Contents         read + write   (read files; write workflows, CLAUDE.md, metrics)
#   Issues           read + write   (the proposal queue: create, label, comment)
#   Pull requests    read + write   (list, update, merge)
#   Actions          read + write   (read runs/logs/artifacts, dispatch workflows)
#   Secrets          read           (checks whether CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN exists
#                                    on a target repo — names only, never values)
#   Workflows        (enable)       (required to write files into .github/workflows/)
#
# The last two are easy to miss and fail in confusing ways when absent.
#
# Use a real fine-grained PAT (github_pat_...). Do NOT paste the output of
# `gh auth token` here — that is your GitHub CLI's OAuth token (gho_...), it
# carries far broader scopes across your whole account, and leaking it means
# revoking your CLI everywhere. They are not interchangeable.
#
# Create one at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------- login security --

# Signs your login cookie. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# If you leave this unset the dashboard falls back to using your password
# (with a warning in the server log) so nothing breaks — but set it.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Bump this number to instantly sign every session out (e.g. after you rotate
# a secret, or if you think someone else got in). Defaults to 1.
# SESSION_KEY_VERSION=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- crons --

# REQUIRED for the 6-hourly reporter cron. The cron endpoint now REFUSES to
# run when this is unset (it used to run wide open to anyone who found the
# URL). Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# On Vercel: set this in Settings -> Environment Variables; Vercel Cron sends
# it automatically. On AWS it moves to an EventBridge Scheduler rule that
# sends "Authorization: Bearer <this value>".
# CRON_SECRET=

# --------------------------------------------------- Mac-only features (!) --

# The launcher / "start from a local folder" features run programs on the
# machine the dashboard is on. They are OFF unless you switch them on here,
# so a cloud deployment can never expose them by accident.
# Set to 1 on YOUR MAC ONLY. Never set this in the cloud.
# LOOP_DASHBOARD_LOCAL_MODE=1

# OPTIONAL — where your local project folders live, for the "start from a
# local folder" option in Add a project. Defaults to your Claude Projects
# folder. Only does anything when LOOP_DASHBOARD_LOCAL_MODE=1.
# CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR=/Users/alessiopagliarulo/Documents/Claude Projects

# --- Public demo mode ------------------------------------------------------

# Set to 1 to let anyone with the link view the dashboard WITHOUT logging in.
#
# What a signed-out visitor gets: the pages, and API reads answered from a
# frozen INVENTED snapshot (lib/demo/*) — the proxy serves those itself, so no
# route handler ever runs for them. Everything else is a 403: every GitHub
# write, every workflow dispatch, every AI/chat route, every config change,
# every launcher route. Signing in is unaffected and restores live data and
# every mutation.
#
# Off unless explicitly set, so a local `next dev` and any private deployment
# keep the password gate. Only the public AWS deployment sets it — see
# infra/task-definition.json. Read lib/public-access.ts before turning it on
# anywhere that has a GITHUB_TOKEN you care about.
# LOOP_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_DEMO=1

# --- AI drafting ("Draft with AI" on the Process Map) and the help chat -----

# Which engine to use. "auto" (the default) picks, in order: the Claude app on
# your Mac -> AWS Bedrock if configured -> the Anthropic API key -> off.
# Force one with: "cli" (Claude app), "bedrock", or "api".
# DASHBOARD_AI_BACKEND=auto

# On your Mac this works out of the box, FOR FREE, through the Claude app
# you're already logged into. The two options below are only for when the
# dashboard runs somewhere there is no Claude app.

# Option 1 — a paid Anthropic API key.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Option 2 — AWS Bedrock. No key: it uses the AWS identity the app already has
# (the ECS task role in the cloud, or your AWS_PROFILE locally). This is the
# option that keeps AI usage inside an AWS account and its CloudTrail log.
# Needs Bedrock model access granted in that region first.
# DASHBOARD_AI_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1

# Which Bedrock API to talk to: "mantle" (default, current) or "invoke" (the
# older InvokeModel path, which uses inference-profile model IDs instead).
# DASHBOARD_AI_BEDROCK_API=mantle

# OPTIONAL — which Claude model to use. Leave these alone unless you have a
# reason to change them. Use a plain model name here (e.g. claude-sonnet-5);
# the Bedrock-specific ID is worked out for you.
# DASHBOARD_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# DASHBOARD_AI_CHAT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# OPTIONAL escape hatches — set an exact Bedrock model ID yourself, bypassing
# the translation above. Only needed if AWS renames something.
# DASHBOARD_AI_BEDROCK_MODEL=
# DASHBOARD_AI_BEDROCK_CHAT_MODEL=
